        "title": "chore(deps): refresh supported toolchain versions",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- update the supported Go toolchain/runtime and compatible Go dependencies, including the maintained `go.yaml.in/yaml/v3` module path\n- refresh the tracking worker toolchain and dependencies, with explicit build-script policy and security overrides for Vite and `ws`\n- update Docker base images and refresh every GitHub Action to an exact, verified upstream SHA\n\n## Compatibility and policy\n\n- hold upstream releases younger than the seven-day stabilization window where applicable\n- retain gofumpt 0.9.2 and golangci-lint 2.11.4 because their latest releases introduce broad unrelated repository churn\n- no public model identifier changes; the Public Model Identifier Gate is not applicable\n- aligned with VISION security and reliability policy; no release or version bump\n\n## Security\n\n- `govulncheck ./...`: clean\n- `pnpm audit`: zero vulnerabilities\n- `ws` is forced to 8.21.0, covering the current security advisory\n\n## Proof\n\n- `make ci`\n- worker `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm build`, and `pnpm test` (15 tests)\n- frozen worker install\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/*.yml`\n- all 12 unique Action SHA pins resolve to their annotated upstream tags\n- Docker build and runtime check on Alpine 3.24.1\n- source-blind CLI behavior contract: 3/3 checks passed\n- autoreview: no accepted or actionable findings\n",
